<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rance</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rance is a river in Brittany, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, about 100 kilometres long, flowing north to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-channel">English Channel</a> between Dinard and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-malo">Saint-Malo</a>. Its long estuary was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> Coriosolites and an important route for medieval Breton trade. The Rance Tidal Power Station, opened across the estuary in 1966, was the world's first large tidal power plant.</p></div>
